   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Word order with weil versus denn",
     "texto": [
      "After **weil** the subordinate clause structure applies: Subject + complements + **conjugated verb at the end**: *Ich nehme den Bus, weil mein Fahrrad kaputt ist* (I'm taking the bus because my bicycle is broken).",
      "If the clause with «weil» comes first: *Weil der Zug Verspätung hat, kommt Herr Müller zu spät* (Since the train is delayed, Mr Müller arrives late).",
      "In contrast, **denn** is a coordinating conjunction that doesn't change the order: the verb stays in second position."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Causal connectors",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Type of link",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Position of the verb",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "weil",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Subordinating",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "At the end of the clause",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "... weil er krank ist.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Weil (at the start)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Initial subordinating",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "At the end; main clause starts with the verb",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Weil er krank ist, bleibt er daheim.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "denn",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
